*	Any value is stored in the memomry of the computer. The smallest unit of memory is a bit (0 or 1). When a value, as 8, is stored 
*	in memory, it is converted in an adress. But the amount of these adresses on the computer is limited, that's why a memory adress
*	holds 1 byte of data. A byte is a group of 8 bites. So the adress of 8 would be "0100 0001".
* 
